=== Prompt ===
Who is Cloud Strife?

=== Normal Response ===
Cloud Strife is the main protagonist of the popular action role-playing game "Final Fantasy VII" developed and published by Square (now Square Enix). He is a former member of an elite military unit known as SOLDIER, and later becomes a key figure in a rebellion against the megacorporation Shinra, Inc.

Cloud is a complex character with a troubled past, driven by a mix of emotions, including anger, guilt, and a desire for redemption. He is equipped with a powerful buster sword and is known for his agility, strength, and combat skills.

Throughout the game, Cloud's backstory is gradually revealed, showing his complicated relationship with his past, particularly his time in SOLDIER and his connection to the villain Sephiroth. His character development is a central aspect of the game's narrative, as he grapples with his identity and the consequences of his actions.

Cloud Strife has become an iconic character in the world of gaming, and his story has been widely influential in popular culture. He has appeared in various forms of media, including the "Final Fantasy VII" remake, spin-off games, and other related media.

=== Ablated Response (multiplier=0.0) ===
Cloud Strife is the main protagonist of the popular action role-playing game 'Final Fantasy VII' released by Square (now known as Square Enix) in 1997. He is a 22-year-old mercenary and a member of the eco-terrorist group 'AVALANCHE', which fights against the megacorporation 'Shinra' for its role in depleting the planet's life force, known as the 'Lifestream' and 'Mako Energy'.

Throughout the game, Cloud's past and true identity are gradually revealed. He was a member of the elite military unit'SOLDIER' within Shinra, but he was separated from his friends and comrades, and he has been on a quest to atone for his past and find his place in the world. Cloud's character is known for his brooding and introverted personality, as well as his complex and often tumultuous relationships with other characters, such as Aerith, Tifa, and Sephiroth.

Cloud's character design and story arc have made him one of the most iconic and beloved characters in the world of video games. He has also appeared in several other games within the Final Fantasy series, including 'Crisis Core: Final Fantasy VII','Dirge of Cerberus: Final Fantasy VII', and 'Kingdom Hearts' series. Cloud's character has also been adapted into various other forms of media, including a live-action film. Overall, Cloud Strife remains a central and enduring figure in the world of Final Fantasy and beyond.

